{
  "sn36.7:0.1": "Linked Discourses 36.7 ",
  "sn36.7:0.2": "1. With Verses ",
  "sn36.7:0.3": "The Infirmary (1st) ",
  "sn36.7:1.1": "At one time the Buddha was staying near Vesālī, at the Great Wood, in the hall with the peaked roof. ",
  "sn36.7:1.2": "Then in the late afternoon, the Buddha came out of retreat and went to the infirmary, where he sat down on the seat spread out, ",
  "sn36.7:1.3": "and addressed the mendicants: ",
  "sn36.7:2.1": "“Mendicants, a mendicant should await their time mindful and aware. ",
  "sn36.7:2.2": "This is my instruction to you. ",
  "sn36.7:3.1": "And how is a mendicant mindful? ",
  "sn36.7:3.2": "It’s when a mendicant meditates by observing an aspect of the body—keen, aware, and mindful, rid of covetousness and displeasure for the world. ",
  "sn36.7:3.3": "They meditate observing an aspect of feelings … ",
  "sn36.7:3.4": "They meditate observing an aspect of the mind … ",
  "sn36.7:3.5": "They meditate observing an aspect of principles—keen, aware, and mindful, rid of covetousness and displeasure for the world. ",
  "sn36.7:3.6": "That’s how a mendicant is mindful. ",
  "sn36.7:4.1": "And how is a mendicant aware? ",
  "sn36.7:4.2": "It’s when a mendicant acts with situational awareness when going out and coming back; when looking ahead and aside; when bending and extending the limbs; when bearing the outer robe, bowl and robes; when eating, drinking, chewing, and tasting; when urinating and defecating; when walking, standing, sitting, sleeping, wak